On 15▇/▇/▇, New Calendar, the Odyssey Ward Police Department (OWPD) reported a high-value jewelry heist and requested our assistance due to the investigation's slow progress.

Case Summary:
According to the OWPD, the suspect is a repeat offender who's recently become active in the area. During encounters with the authorities, she identified herself as Black Crow, the Phantom Thief. Judging by her slim build and quick movements, she's believed to be an adult female.

The night before the heist, the suspect sent a calling card announcing she would steal a famous painting from a private residence. This successfully drew a large portion of the police to that location, while she slipped into another manor at midnight.

Surveillance footage from the victim's estate shows the thief bypassing the outer walls through unknown means, evading all security systems, and heading straight to the basement, where she stole a priceless diamond known as the "Eye of the Goddess."

When the alarm was triggered as she broke the display case, security personnel rushed in and tried to intercept her—but she managed to escape without a trace.

Investigation Details:
We attempted to recover footage from surrounding streets and nearby surveillance points in Odyssey Ward, but there was no sign of Black Crow's arrival or departure.

Local patrols were reinforced, and we assisted the OWPD in nightly sweeps, hoping to catch her in the act. However, she went quiet for an entire month. The operation was eventually called off due to resource strain. Naturally, the very next day after our withdrawal, another manor was hit.

We set multiple traps to lure her out, but the suspect was far too cautious and never took the bait.

We also tried tracing the stolen items, but not a single one has reappeared.

We attempted...

Conclusion:
As of 15▇/▇/▇, New Calendar, after ▇ months of pursuit, Black Crow's whereabouts remain unknown. A request has been submitted to raise the case's priority level.
On 15▇/▇/▇, New Calendar, the case was officially reassigned. This report is now closed.

